# Winning a travel encounter that fired on the journey's LAST step finishes the journey.
#
# This is the softlock a playtester reported as "the game froze after we killed a wolf": the travel
# progress box left standing over a black screen, with nothing but the pause menu to escape by.
#
# The last step of a path raises ProtagonistSteppedToVertex and ProtagonistArrivedAtLocation from the
# SAME MicroworldInterface.UpdateMovement call, and clears the path between the two. So an encounter
# rolled there begins with the arrival ALREADY announced — and OnProtagonistArrived dropped it,
# because the mode had just become EncounterPrompt. Win the fight, and travel resumes onto a path
# that no longer exists: Traveling for ever. LocationInteraction below is the whole assertion.
#
# --encounter-on-arrival stages exactly that step; a random roll reaches it about once in a hundred
# journeys, which is why the flag exists. It is honoured ahead of --no-encounters, so the random
# rolls stay off and this one still fires.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --encounter-on-arrival wolf

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60

# Somewhere, anywhere — the destination does not matter, only that the trip ends.
travel neighbour
travel-go

wait mode EncounterPrompt 90
click engage
wait mode Fighting 90

fight-end victory

# The journey finishes itself: the held arrival is delivered and the location opens.
# Before the fix this sat in Traveling until the run timed out.
wait mode LocationInteraction 90

quit
